  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Relief Food Appeal for Drought Affected Kenyans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya government has declared more than 3.1 million Kenyans are facing high levels of acute food insecurity, widespread livelihood loses and displacement in 23 ASAL counties. 2,400 people in East Pokot alone are in emergency state - a familiar sites and memories of low-pitched cries accompanying distressed furrow brow and smelling decomposing carcasses. East Pokot is predominantly inhabited pastoralists and severe vegetation deficits  increases vulnerability to climate shocks and stresses.</narrative>
  </description>
